{{- $c := .Local -}}
{{- $cliName := $c.CliName -}}
{{- $b := $c.Body -}}
{{- if $b}}
Commands that accept a request body take it three ways, with a clear priority chain. The examples use `{{$b.Command}}`; every body-bearing command works the same way{{if $b.HasSchema}} and prints its exact request schema with `--schema`{{end}}.
{{- if $b.HasFlags}}

### Individual flags (highest priority)

Each top-level body field is a flag:

```bash
{{$b.Command}}{{range $b.Flags}} {{.Arg}}{{end}}
```
{{- end}}

### `--{{$b.BodyFlag}}` flag

Provide the entire request body as a JSON string:

```bash
{{$b.Command}} --{{$b.BodyFlag}} '{{$b.BodyJSON}}'
```
{{- if $b.FirstFlag}}

Individual flags override `--{{$b.BodyFlag}}` values:

```bash
# Sends {{$b.FirstFlagOverrideJSON}}
{{$b.Command}} --{{$b.BodyFlag}} '{{$b.BodyJSON}}' {{$b.OverrideValue}}
```
{{- end}}

### Stdin piping (lowest priority)

Pipe JSON into any command that accepts a request body:

```bash
echo '{{$b.BodyJSON}}' | {{$b.Command}}
```
{{- if $b.FirstFlag}}

Individual flags override stdin values:

```bash
# Sends {{$b.FirstFlagOverrideJSON}}
echo '{{$b.BodyJSON}}' | {{$b.Command}} {{$b.OverrideValue}}
```
{{- end}}

This is useful for chaining commands, reading from files, or scripting:

```bash
# Read body from a file
{{$b.Command}} < request.json

# Pipe from another command
curl -s https://example.com/request.json | {{$b.Command}}
```

### Priority

When multiple input methods are used, the priority is:

| Priority | Source | Description |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| 1 (highest) | Individual flags | {{if $b.FirstFlag}}`--{{$b.FirstFlag.Flag}} ...`{{else}}A field flag{{end}} always wins |
| 2 | `--{{$b.BodyFlag}}` flag | Whole-body JSON via flag |
| 3 (lowest) | Stdin | Piped JSON input |
{{- else}}
Commands that accept a request body take it three ways, with a clear priority chain: individual field flags (highest priority), the whole body as JSON via `--body`, and JSON piped on stdin (lowest priority). Later sources never override earlier ones{{if $c.Schema}}; a body-bearing command prints its exact request schema with `--schema`{{end}}.
{{- end}}
